Author: Kel Modderman <kelvmod@gmail.com>
Description: Queue terminal output instead of waiting for room.
 terminal-nonblocking.patch waits in poll() while a terminal drains, so a
 slow terminal stalls the event loop until it drains, a wedged one for a
 second per write, and one slow terminal delays the others. Queue what the
 terminal can't take and write it as it drains, from an event loop watch.
 Graphics mode, termios changes and close drain the queue first, waiting
 at most a second without progress; a hangup drops it. The queue is a
 ply_buffer_t, capped at about 1 MiB.
Bug-Debian: https://bugs.debian.org/1145446
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-10

